1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,500
Every month, millions of workers in Ivory Coast get a payslip they cannot read.

2
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:15,000
CNPS, ITS, CMU. Since the 2024 tax reform, mistakes are common, and almost nobody notices them.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Uploading your payslip to an AI means sending your salary to a server.

4
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:32,000
PayslipLens does the opposite. Gemini Nano, the AI built into Chrome, reads the payslip on your device. Your salary never leaves it.

5
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:40,000
I drop a payslip. Firebase AI Logic runs Gemini Nano in on-device only mode, so this call cannot fall back to the cloud.

6
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Nano extracts the figures as JSON, without names or IDs.

7
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Then plain code checks the law, with exact math.

8
00:00:52,000 --> 00:01:01,000
Here PayslipLens finds two errors: the CNPS was computed on the wrong base, including the transport allowance,

9
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:08,000
and the income tax ignores the family reduction for three tax parts.

10
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:13,000
That is about twenty-five thousand francs too much, every month.

11
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:20,000
I can change my family situation, and the check updates at once.

12
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Any line can be explained. This line contains real amounts,

13
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:42,000
so the explanation is also generated by Gemini Nano, on the device, streamed as it is written.

14
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:50,000
For a deeper legal answer, I ask the cloud. But first, PayslipLens shows me exactly what will leave my device:

15
00:01:50,000 --> 00:02:00,000
a salary band, percentages, the check results, and my question with numbers masked. No name, no exact amount.

16
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:15,000
Only then is it sent to Gemini in the cloud, in prefer-in-cloud mode.

17
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:24,000
Under the hood, the inference mode follows the sensitivity of the data. On-device only for the payslip, prefer cloud for anonymized questions,

18
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:31,000
and cloud only with explicit consent when a browser has no Nano.

19
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:40,000
App Check protects the API, Remote Config updates the tax rates without a release, and it is all open source.

20
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:48,000
PayslipLens helps workers check what they are owed, without giving up their privacy.

21
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:55,000
Try it at payslip-lens dot web dot app.
